{"title":"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Alcumus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Alcumus)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a standard die one of the dots is removed at random with each dot equally likely to be chosen. The die is then rolled. What is the probability that the top face has an odd number of dots?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3406352af3df9d499b2d67eea7973faa18f52eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\mathrm {A}) \\ \\frac{5}{11} \\qquad (\\mathrm {B}) \\ \\frac{10}{21} \\qquad (\\mathrm {C})\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad (\\mathrm {D}) \\ \\frac{11}{21} \\qquad (\\mathrm {E})\\ \\frac{6}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"397\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20745808207d57826105237893b01c6565892e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"207\" height=\"14\" /> dots total. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Casework\" title=\"Casework\">Casework</a>:\n</p>\n<ul><li>The dot is removed from an even face. There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/9888556452915fb9ef1dc3b0bd3a2d781610ca39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2+4+6}{21} = \\frac{4}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" /> chance of this happening. Then there are 4 odd faces, giving us a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e215fb812d234f27ef19a4288cc89eb912b2722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 47 \\cdot \\frac 46 = \\frac{8}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />.</li>\n<li>The dot is removed from an odd face. There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7571c97327fc18eb94ff75f7f18bbf98d102e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+3+5}{21} = \\frac{3}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" /> chance of this happening. Then there are 2 odd faces, giving us a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a2fe8185286808ef44348c133bde4a01eab719c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 37 \\cdot \\frac 26 = \\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f24ebd49dd907fb661b1bef66e16a605868321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 8{21} + \\frac 17 = \\frac{11}{21} \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Alcumus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Alcumus)\">Solution 2 (Alcumus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Alcumus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The probability that the top face is odd is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/217aedbdc339bacc8ba075a2ec16902b098194e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> if a dot is removed from an odd face, and the probability that the top face is odd is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38bd36e353df831303c0de895a9ec614cf3e7202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> if a dot is removed from an even face. Because each dot has the probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d1feea8e24a5f3194b6b26b10d82e5ace018ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> of being removed, the top face is odd with probability<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac22e91ae3dd05614b25788bc82bdc698b8d3e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1+3+5}{21}\\right) +\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2+4+6}{21}\\right) = \\frac{33}{63} = \\boxed{\\frac{11}{21}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"416\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A\">2005 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/